paras.en:
When the king of religion entered Karbala,
the desert of trial became a model of the highest Paradise.
The sky’s head bowed; this was the elevation of earth;
the sun was lost in the beauty of beautiful Husayn.
It gained lustre from the appearance of the sun of the faith;
the moons attached themselves to the wilderness by the light of his face.

By the fragrance of those flowers the desert became garden upon garden;
buds opened, the scars of the nightingale’s heart turned green.
The pride of every mountain reached the head of the sky;
the river too lit lamps of bubbles.
The layers of the holy earth became suns;
the particles of dust made the stars into dust.
